module getar_match_over_let_construct_panics

// PRD `docs/prds/v0_6/generic-enum-type-arg-retention.md` — leaf ε RED
// before-image (defect P-1). MEASURED 2026-09-29 with target/debug/reify
// built 2026-09-25 (main 300910857b):
//   `reify check` EXIT 101, `reify eval` EXIT 101 — both PANIC at
//   crates/reify-eval/src/engine_eval.rs `is_representable_cell_type`:
//   "unrepresentable cell_type: value cell `W.v` has cell_type TypeParam("T")".
// Path: the `let r` cell takes the initializer's erased type `Enum("Result")`;
// the match discriminant therefore has an empty binder substitution; binder
// `x` is typed `TypeParam("T")`; the match's result type is the first arm's
// body type, so `let v` is typed `TypeParam("T")`, which the debug-build
// representability assert rejects.
// RELEASE build (target/release/reify, 2026-09-01): `reify check` EXIT 0,
// `reify eval` EXIT 0 printing `W.v = 0.005 m` — the runtime value is RIGHT;
// only the static cell type is wrong (TypeParam("T")), which the release
// profile never checks. The probe harness prefers target/release/reify but
// honours REIFY_BIN, so the POST-state probe must run with
// REIFY_BIN=target/debug/reify on a REBUILT debug binary; its dispatch-time
// cover is a Rust-level debug-profile test asserting the let cell's
// cell_type is Scalar[m], with the fixture registered in
// `_RUST_COUPLED_RI_FIXTURES`. δ alone closes THIS file (the Ok arm comes
// first and T is bound); the R5 rule is exercised by
// getar_match_err_first_arm_panics.ri instead.
// EXPECTED after δ (debug build): `reify check` EXIT 0; `reify eval` prints `W.v = 0.005 m`.

structure def W {
    let r = Ok { value: 5mm }
    let v = match r { Ok { value: x } => x, Err { error: e } => 1mm }
}
